From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:49:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix test build with CMake 4

CHECK_TYPE_SIZE defaults to the C language, but the test subproject only
enables CXX. CMake 4 rejects try_compile() with a .c source when C is not
an enabled language, so configuring with -DPLOG_BUILD_TESTS=ON fails:

    CMake Error at CheckIncludeFile.cmake:157 (try_compile):
      Unknown extension ".c" for file .../CheckIncludeFile.c
      try_compile() works only for enabled languages.

The type check is trivial C++-compatible code, so run it in CXX.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-11
---
 test/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/CMakeLists.txt b/test/CMakeLists.txt
index e988660..01107d9 100644
--- a/test/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ set(SOURCES
 #
 
 include(CheckTypeSize)
-CHECK_TYPE_SIZE(wchar_t PLOG_SIZEOF_WCHAR)
+CHECK_TYPE_SIZE(wchar_t PLOG_SIZEOF_WCHAR LANGUAGE CXX)
 
 #
 # Test creation functions to avoid code duplication